      "hints": [
        "Differentiate $y = 4(5 - 3x)^{-1}$ to get $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 12(5 - 3x)^{-2}$.",
        "At $x = 1$, $y = 2$, tangent gradient is $3 \\implies$ normal gradient $-\\frac{1}{3}$.",
        "Form normal equation $y = -\\frac{1}{3}x + \\frac{7}{3}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Differentiate $y = 4(5 - 3x)^{-1}$ using the chain rule:\n$$\\frac{dy}{dx} = 4(-1)(5 - 3x)^{-2}(-3) = 12(5 - 3x)^{-2} = \\frac{12}{(5 - 3x)^2}$$",
        "Evaluate the curve point and tangent gradient at $x = 1$:\n$$y_1 = \\frac{4}{5 - 3(1)} = \\frac{4}{2} = 2$$\n$$m_T = \\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=1} = \\frac{12}{(5 - 3(1))^2} = \\frac{12}{2^2} = 3$$\n$$m_N = -\\frac{1}{m_T} = -\\frac{1}{3}$$",
        "Write the equation of the normal line at $(1, 2)$:\n$$y - 2 = -\\frac{1}{3}(x - 1) \\implies y = -\\frac{1}{3}x + \\frac{1}{3} + 2 \\implies y = -\\frac{1}{3}x + \\frac{7}{3}$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "ai_rubric": {
          "Normal Line Equation": "Differentiates to $\\frac{12}{(5-3x)^2}$ (B2). Finds point $(1, 2)$ and $m_T = 3$ (M1). Finds $m_N = -1/3$ (DM1). States $y = -\\frac{1}{3}x + \\frac{7}{3}$ (A1)."
        },
        "criteria_source": "mark_scheme_structured"
