      "hints": [
        "Volume formula: $V = \\pi \\int_0^1 16(5 - 3x)^{-2} dx = \\frac{16\\pi}{3} \\left[ \\frac{1}{5 - 3x} \\right]_0^1$.",
        "Evaluate at $1$ and $0$: $\\frac{16\\pi}{3}\\left(\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{1}{5}\\right) = \\frac{8\\pi}{5}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Set up the volume of revolution integral for the region bounded by $x = 0$ to $x = 1$:\n$$V = \\pi \\int_0^1 y^2\\,dx = \\pi \\int_0^1 \\left(\\frac{4}{5 - 3x}\\right)^2 dx = 16\\pi \\int_0^1 (5 - 3x)^{-2}\\,dx$$",
        "Integrate using the reverse chain rule:\n$$V = 16\\pi \\left[ \\frac{(5 - 3x)^{-1}}{(-1)(-3)} \\right]_0^1 = \\frac{16\\pi}{3} \\left[ \\frac{1}{5 - 3x} \\right]_0^1$$",
        "Evaluate at the limits $x = 1$ and $x = 0$:\n$$V = \\frac{16\\pi}{3} \\left( \\frac{1}{5 - 3(1)} - \\frac{1}{5 - 3(0)} \\right) = \\frac{16\\pi}{3} \\left( \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{1}{5} \\right)$$\n$$= \\frac{16\\pi}{3} \\left( \\frac{3}{10} \\right) = \\frac{48\\pi}{30} = \\frac{8\\pi}{5} \\quad (\\approx 5.03)$$"
      ],
